-{"attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocked_since": null, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["engine", "what-if"], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "completed_at": null, "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-09-22T04:57:09.789450+00:00", "depends_on": [], "dispatched_at": null, "exit_code": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": "Real-use P1 from the dogfood run; the what-if engine is the flagship and this silently corrupts its output.", "guard_result": null, "id": "AUG-015", "lines_added": null, "lines_removed": null, "perpetual": false, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "priority": 1, "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-22 real-use run", "review_notes": null, "status": "pending", "title": "[P1] toggle has no per-decision exclusivity: two options of one decision can be active and dump renders both as THE configuration", "updated_at": "2026-09-22T04:57:09.789450+00:00", "worker_status": null, "worker_summary": null, "detail": "Reproduced 2026-09-22 on a throwaway namespace (auger-dogfood-df1): answer D-001 with 3 options, then `toggle --on D-001-O3` -> stored state has BOTH D-001-O1 (chosen) and O3 active=true; plain `dump` then prints \"ACTIVE CONFIGURATION: D-001=stream..., D-001=grep...\" — one decision bound to two contradictory choices. The option register exists precisely so a configuration is a SELECTION across alternatives; cmd_toggle (auger.py ~2003) is a raw PATCH with no invariant, and dump composes every active option without noticing the collision. Fix direction: toggle --on should default to flipping the sibling options off (an --additive escape hatch if ever needed), and dump/status should WARN when a decision has !=1 active option."}
